@* The root of /strict-csp, which App.razor renders in place of Routes and the server serves with a
   Content-Security-Policy whose style-src has no 'unsafe-inline' (Program.cs). Every Bheadless
   component under it runs in strict CSP mode (BitBhOptions.StrictCsp, cascaded here so the rest of the
   site keeps the default mode): no style attribute in the markup, the styles applied through the
   CSSOM by bit-bheadless-csp.js. The E2E suite (StrictCspTests) fails on any violation the policy
   reports, so a component that renders a style attribute again is caught there.

   No site chrome: the header, the docs shell and the samples of the other pages are not rendered in
   strict mode, and their own style attributes would be refused. The .page / .bb-docs-content
   wrappers are the ones the E2E suite waits on and searches in. *@

<CascadingValue Value="_options" IsFixed="true">
    <div class="page strict-csp" data-interactive="@(RendererInfo.IsInteractive ? "true" : "false")">
        <main id="csp-main" tabindex="-1">
            <div class="bb-docs-content">
                <StrictCspPage />
            </div>
        </main>
    </div>
    <BitBhPortalOutlet />
</CascadingValue>

@code {
    private readonly BitBhOptions _options = new() { StrictCsp = true };
}
